<code>assert index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size()) => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i-1)));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert index >= 0 && index <= \old(size) => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(size); (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i-1)));</code>

This assert statement captures the condition that for every valid index from the insertion point to the old size of the list, the element at each subsequent index in the updated list is either null and was null in the old list, or is equal to the element at the previous index in the old list.
--------------------
<code>assert index >= 0 && index <= \old(size) => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(size); (this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i-1))) || (\old(this.get(i)) == null && this.get(i) == null));</code>

This assert statement captures the condition that for every valid index from the insertion point to the old size of the list, the element at each subsequent index in the updated list is either equal to the element at the previous index in the old list or both are null.
--------------------
